Fillets: where the face at a spine's end cuts an analytic blend to a point
on an edge of that face (ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd), the point's parameters on a
periodic face are taken in the period of the cut's other end, the blend's
contact on the edge it crossed into the face, instead of the edge's own
(mitcad#1422).

The plate's top edge rounded up to a boss whose cylinder the plate's side
goes on into tangentially, the cylinder's seam running up from the vertex
on the vertical edge the cut ends on: that edge's curve on the cylinder
lies on the seam's one side (u = 5 pi / 2), the cut runs from it to the
foot on the other (u = 2.07 at 3): its curve on the cylinder was made a
period off (from 7.85 to 8.35) and the face's wire did not close in its
parameters (an unorientable face).

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_boss_tangent.cpp, the plate's top edge
picked at its other side rounded with 1, 3 and 6 on the synthetic body
whose seam runs up at the side picked first (y = 25).

Upstream: new.

